                        "glosses": [
                            "A male given name from the Celtic languages, variant of Tristan."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8101b864-2bbd-4356-ac74-fc831d5698db",
                                "sense_id": "e9c5a833-04d1-33ae-ac7f-c080d588225b",
                                "text": "But of all names in the universe he had the most unconquerable aversion for Tristram;--he had the lowest and most contemptible opinion of it of any thing in the world,--thinking it could possibly produce nothing in rerum natura, but what was extremely mean and pitiful: - - - --In a word, to behold such a one, in his old age, ill-fitted for troubles, ten times in a day suffering sorrow;--ten times in a day calling the child of his prayers Tristram!-- Melancholy dissyllable of sound! which, to his ears, was unison to Nincompoop, and every name vituperative under heaven."
                            }
                        ]
